                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote><p>Text is relatively neat and even, although the letters are significantly crowded on the stone, leading to a rather blocky shape to the incised letters. Use of triangular interpuncts. Serifs are prominent. In line 1 of the footer, the first "L" is much taller than the rest of the line; this is repeated in the "L" of his filiation, as well as the "F" of "f(ilius)" in the same line</p>
